        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "There's also the issue that the average damage for any of the dice used (d4, d6, d8, d10, d12) will NOT be an integer.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nExpected tries to kill [table] [tr][td]AtkDie↓ Lt Die→[/td][td]d4[/td][td]d6[/td][td]d8[/td][td]d10[/td][td]d12[/td][/tr] [tr][td]d4[/td][td]2.67[/td][td]6.67[/td][td]12.00[/td][td]18.67[/td][td]26.67[/td][/tr] [tr][td]d6[/td][td]4.80[/td][td]12.00[/td][td]21.60[/td][td]33.60[/td][td]48.00[/td][/tr] [tr][td]d8[/td][td]4.57[/td][td]11.43[/td][td]20.57[/td][td]32.00[/td][td]45.71[/td][/tr] [tr][td]d10[/td][td]2.67[/td][td]6.00[/td][td]10.44[/td][td]16.00[/td][td]22.67[/td][/tr] [tr][td]d12[/td][td]2.09[/td][td]4.49[/td][td]7.40[/td][td]11.03[/td][td]15.40[/td][/tr][/table]\n\nI worked this out by count-table rather than pure formula. (makes it easier to replicate the rules - damage die ≤&nbsp; lieutenant die is no drop).\n\nThe OP's data looks closer to expected tries to step-down...\n\n[table] Expected tries to stepdown [tr][td]AtkDie↓ Lt Die→[/td][td]d4[/td][td]d6[/td][td]d8[/td][td]d10[/td][td]d12[/td][/tr] [tr][td]d4[/td][td]2.67[/td][td]4.00[/td][td]5.33[/td][td]6.67[/td][td]8.00[/td][/tr] [tr][td]d6[/td][td]4.80[/td][td]7.20[/td][td]9.60[/td][td]12.00[/td][td]14.40[/td][/tr] [tr][td]d8[/td][td]4.57[/td][td]6.86[/td][td]9.14[/td][td]11.43[/td][td]13.71[/td][/tr] [tr][td]d10[/td][td]2.67[/td][td]3.33[/td][td]4.44[/td][td]5.56[/td][td]6.67[/td][/tr] [tr][td]d12[/td][td]2.09[/td][td]2.40[/td][td]2.91[/td][td]3.64[/td][td]4.36[/td][/tr][/table]\n\nWorksheet: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Y9UYSxj8k2RmS7Z98UbCrqFVmVLBeV7R8og76fwiPrI/edit?usp=sharing\n",
